const path = '/kindle-colorsoft-case/';
const title = 'Kindle Colorsoft Case: Fit for 2024, 2025 and 2026 Models';
const description = 'Find a Kindle Colorsoft case that fits: 2024 Signature Edition, 2025 16 GB and the new 2026 Colorsoft compared, plus Double Tap, wireless charging and color-screen notes.';

const faq = [
  { q: `Do Kindle Paperwhite cases fit the Kindle Colorsoft?`, a: `A case for the 2024 Paperwhite usually does, and a case for any other Paperwhite does not. Amazon lists identical outer dimensions for the 2024 Paperwhite and the 2024 Colorsoft Signature Edition (127.6 × 176.7 × 7.8 mm), and Amazon's own plant-based leather case is listed for the 2024 Paperwhite, the Colorsoft and the Colorsoft Signature Edition. The 2021 Paperwhite is a smaller 6.8-inch body, and the 2026 Paperwhite and Colorsoft are a new, thinner design. Buy a case whose title names your Colorsoft, not just "Paperwhite."` },
  { q: `Will a 2024 Colorsoft case fit the 2026 Colorsoft?`, a: `We have no evidence that it will, and two reasons to doubt it. WIRED gives the 2026 Colorsoft as 6.8 mm thick, against Amazon's 7.8 mm for the 2024 model, and The Verge reports that the 2026 models moved the power button from the bottom to the right edge near the top, so the cutouts and the fit differ. We found no published width and height for the 2026 Colorsoft yet. Wait for a listing that names the 2026 model, or start with one of Amazon's 2026 covers.` },
  { q: `Is a Kindle Colorsoft case the same as a Kindle Scribe Colorsoft case?`, a: `No, and this is the easiest mistake to make. The Kindle Colorsoft is a 7-inch e-reader; the Kindle Scribe Colorsoft is an 11-inch writing tablet at 189 × 245 × 5.4 mm with a magnetic pen on the side. Their cases are not interchangeable. Search results for "Colorsoft case" mix both, so check the screen size in the title. For the Scribe, use our <a href="/kindle-scribe-case/#y2025">Scribe case guide</a>.` },
  { q: `Does a case affect the Colorsoft's color screen?`, a: `We found no Amazon statement or independent test saying it does. A folio covers the screen only when it is closed; when open, the case wraps the back and frame. What Amazon does say is that the Colorsoft display adds a color filter layer, so its texture or brightness can look different from a Paperwhite's, and that its covers have a microfiber interior to help protect the screen from scratches. A screen protector is a different matter, and there we found listings but no tests of how one affects color or glare.` },
  { q: `Does Double Tap work with a case on?`, a: `Amazon's user guide for the 2024 Colorsoft says the Signature Edition's Double Tap feature, which turns the page when you tap the side or back twice, "has been tested with the official Amazon Kindle Colorsoft case, but may not work with all third party cases." A thick or very soft case could plausibly dampen the taps, but we have not tested any. If you use Double Tap, Amazon's case is the one option Amazon says was tested.` },
  { q: `Can I wirelessly charge my Colorsoft in a case?`, a: `Only the 2024 Colorsoft Signature Edition supports Qi wireless charging; Amazon's 2025 announcement says wireless charging is one of the things the Signature Edition adds over the 16 GB model. Amazon's wireless dock states a 4 mm case limit, and Amazon's safety text says to keep metallic or magnetic objects, including metallic cases, off a wireless charger. The 2026 Colorsoft Signature Edition uses a pogo-pin dock instead, so a case must leave the pins on the back clear.` },
  { q: `Do the Colorsoft 16 GB and the Signature Edition use the same case?`, a: `Amazon's own plant-based leather case lists both the "Kindle Colorsoft" and the "Kindle Colorsoft Signature Edition," which suggests a shared body for the 2024 and 2025 models, but we did not find separate published dimensions for the 16 GB model. For the 2026 generation, the Signature Edition has an aluminum back and pogo pins, and Amazon also sells slim magnetic-attach covers for aluminum models, so check that a 2026 case names your exact edition.` },
  { q: `How much is Amazon's official Colorsoft case?`, a: `When we checked on ${FACTS_AS_OF_OCT5}, Amazon's plant-based leather case for the 2024 Paperwhite and Colorsoft was listed at $42.99 in Raspberry, with prices varying by color and seller. For the 2026 lineup, Amazon's announcement lists Kindle Covers from $39.99 and the Page-Turn Cover at $79.99 for the Signature Editions. Prices change often; the Amazon listing is the source of truth.` },
];
const ld = [
  article({ headline: title, description, path, published: PUBLISHED_OCT5 }),
  breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Kindle case', path: '/kindle-case/' }, { name: 'Kindle Colorsoft case', path }]),
  faqPage(faq),
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} jsonld={ld} ogType="article">
  <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/kindle-case/">Kindle cases</a> › Kindle Colorsoft case</p>
  <h1>Kindle Colorsoft Case: Which One Fits Your Colorsoft</h1>
  <p class="meta">Facts checked {FACTS_AS_OF_OCT5}. Independent guide based on Amazon's listings, user guides and announcements plus press coverage. We have not hands-on tested any case mentioned.</p>
  <Disclosure />

  <p class="lede">"Kindle Colorsoft" now covers four different devices: the original 2024 Signature Edition, a cheaper 16 GB model from 2025, a redesigned 2026 Colorsoft that ships at the end of October, and the much larger Kindle Scribe Colorsoft. A case that fits one may not fit the next. This guide sorts out which Colorsoft you have, which cases are made for it, and the few things about a color Kindle that change what to look for in a case, such as Double Tap, wireless charging and the pogo pins on the 2026 Signature Edition.</p>

  <div class="box">
    <h2 id="short">Short answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>2024 Colorsoft Signature Edition or 2025 Colorsoft 16 GB:</strong> look for cases that name the Colorsoft. Amazon gives the 2024 Colorsoft the same outer size as the 2024 Paperwhite, and Amazon's own case is listed for both, so 2024 Paperwhite cases that also name the Colorsoft are the usual choice.</li>
      <li><strong>2026 Colorsoft:</strong> a thinner new body (6.8 mm) with the power button moved to the right edge. Do not reuse a 2024 case. Wait for listings that name the 2026 model, or start with Amazon's 2026 covers.</li>
      <li><strong>Kindle Scribe Colorsoft (11-inch):</strong> a different device entirely. Use the <a href="/kindle-scribe-case/#y2025">Scribe case guide</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Signature Edition owners:</strong> check that the case keeps Double Tap working, and that it suits wireless charging (2024) or leaves the pogo pins clear (2026).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <strong>On this page</strong>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#identify">Which Colorsoft do you have?</a></li>
      <li><a href="#by-model">Colorsoft models compared</a></li>
      <li><a href="#y2024">2024 and 2025 Colorsoft cases</a></li>
      <li><a href="#y2026">2026 Colorsoft cases</a></li>
      <li><a href="#color">What a color screen changes about choosing a case</a></li>
      <li><a href="#signature">Signature Edition features and cases</a></li>
      <li><a href="#official">Amazon's own Colorsoft cases</a></li>
      <li><a href="#styles">Case styles for a Colorsoft</a></li>
      <li><a href="#scribe">Kindle Scribe Colorsoft</a></li>
      <li><a href="#red-flags">Colorsoft case red flags</a></li>
      <li><a href="#method">How we researched this</a></li>
      <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="identify">Which Colorsoft do you have?</h2>
  <p>Start here, because the name alone does not tell a case seller which body you own.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>7-inch, power button on the bottom edge, launched 2024:</strong> the Kindle Colorsoft Signature Edition. Amazon's listing calls it "Kindle Colorsoft Signature Edition (1st Generation) – 2024 release." It has 32 GB, an auto-adjusting front light and Qi wireless charging.</li>
    <li><strong>The same shape, 16 GB, launched July 24, 2025:</strong> the Kindle Colorsoft 16 GB. Amazon's announcement says the Signature Edition adds an auto-adjusting front light, wireless charging and 32 GB over it. The Kindle Colorsoft Kids launched the same day with its own kid-friendly cover included.</li>
    <li><strong>7-inch with the power button on the right edge, near the top:</strong> the 2026 Kindle Colorsoft or Colorsoft Signature Edition, announced October 1, 2026 and shipping October 28. The Verge reports the button moved across the new lineup; the Signature Edition has an aluminum back with pogo pins.</li>
    <li><strong>11-inch with a pen:</strong> the Kindle Scribe Colorsoft (2025). See the <a href="#scribe">Scribe Colorsoft section</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To confirm, the Kindle's Device Info screen in settings shows the device's name and generation, according to Amazon's user guides, and so does your device list in your Amazon account. The release year is the safer matching key than any generation number.</p>

  <ColorsoftFit />

  <h2 id="by-model">Colorsoft models compared</h2>
  <Table
    caption="Colorsoft models and what matters for a case. Sizes and weights from Amazon unless noted."
    head={['Model', 'Screen', 'Outer size', 'Weight', 'Charging', 'Case notes']}
    rows={[
      [`Colorsoft Signature Edition (2024)`, `7-inch`, `127.6 × 176.7 × 7.8 mm`, `219 g`, `USB-C; Qi wireless; Amazon wireless dock`, `Same outer size as the 2024 Paperwhite per Amazon; Double Tap`],
      [`Colorsoft 16 GB (2025)`, `7-inch`, `Not published separately in our sources`, `Not found`, `USB-C only`, `Amazon's case lists "Kindle Colorsoft" alongside the Signature Edition`],
      [`Colorsoft and Colorsoft Signature (2026)`, `7-inch`, `6.8 mm thick; width and height not confirmed`, `204 g (per WIRED; edition not specified)`, `Signature: USB-C and pogo-pin dock, no Qi (The Verge); standard model's port not confirmed`, `New body, power button on right edge; Signature has pogo pins and Double Tap; Page-Turn Cover for Signature only`],
      [`Scribe Colorsoft (2025)`, `11-inch`, `189 × 245 × 5.4 mm`, `400 g`, `USB-C`, `Writing tablet with magnetic pen; see the <a href="/kindle-scribe-case/#y2025">Scribe guide</a>`],
    ]}
  />
  <p>Two cautions on the table. First, we could not confirm the 2026 Colorsoft's width and height or the Signature Edition's weight in Amazon's materials or reliable coverage; one blog's figures, as they appeared in search results, did not add up, so we leave them out. Second, the 2024 Colorsoft weighs 8 g more than the 2024 Paperwhite (219 g against 211 g, both Amazon figures), which does not change the fit of a case made for the shared body.</p>

  <h2 id="y2024">2024 and 2025 Colorsoft cases</h2>
  <p>For the 2024 Signature Edition, the fit question is simpler than it looks. Amazon gives exactly the same outer dimensions for it and for the 2024 Paperwhite, 127.6 × 176.7 × 7.8 mm, and Amazon's plant-based leather case says it is "compatible with Kindle Paperwhite, Kindle Paperwhite Signature Edition (Fits 2024 Release Only), Kindle Colorsoft and Kindle Colorsoft Signature Edition." Third-party accessory makers group them the same way: for example, a tempered-glass screen protector sold at Best Buy is titled for the "Kindle Paperwhite 2024 and Colorsoft." That is why our <a href="/kindle-paperwhite-case/#y2024">2024 Paperwhite case section</a> notes that many 2024 listings also name the Colorsoft.</p>
  <p>Our advice still is to buy a case whose title names the Colorsoft, not just "Paperwhite." Same outer dimensions do not guarantee that a seller has checked the cutouts, the magnet position for auto sleep/wake, or the fit around the Signature Edition's features. Recent reviews from Colorsoft owners, searched for "Colorsoft," "fit" and "button," are the best check we know of.</p>
  <p>The 2025 Colorsoft 16 GB is where we have less to go on. Amazon's case listing names the "Kindle Colorsoft" as well as the Signature Edition, and Amazon's announcement describes the difference from the Signature Edition in features (front light, wireless charging, storage) rather than size, but we did not find a separate dimension listing for it. Treat a case that names both as the safe choice.</p>
  <p>What about older Paperwhite cases? A 2021 Paperwhite case will not do: the 2021 model is a 6.8-inch body of about 124.6 × 174 × 8.1 mm in our <a href="/kindle-paperwhite-case/#y2021">Paperwhite case guide</a>, smaller than the Colorsoft.</p>
  <p><a class="btn alt" href={amazonSearch('kindle colorsoft case 2024')} rel={LINK_REL} target="_blank">Search Amazon: 2024 Colorsoft cases</a></p>

  <h2 id="y2026">2026 Colorsoft cases</h2>
  <p>Amazon announced a redesigned Colorsoft on October 1, 2026: a 16 GB model at $289.99 in Graphite and a Signature Edition at $319.99 in Graphite and Fig, with an aluminum housing, 32 GB, an auto-adjusting front light, Double Tap and pogo-pin dock charging. WIRED gives both the Paperwhite and the Colorsoft as 6.8 mm thick and 204 g. Pre-orders open on a rolling basis and the devices ship October 28, 2026.</p>
  <p>For cases, that adds up to a new body. It is a full millimeter thinner than the 2024 Colorsoft, The Verge reports the power button moved from the bottom to the right edge near the top, and Amazon describes a flush-front display with color that "wraps seamlessly from front to back." A 2024 case would at best be loose and at worst cover the button, so do not reuse one.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Amazon's 2026 covers:</strong> Kindle Covers from $39.99 in knit fabric, plant-based leather and pebbled premium leather that "wrap fully around the device," color-matched across the lineup.</li>
    <li><strong>Slim magnetic-attach covers:</strong> Amazon says these are also available for devices with aluminum housing, which includes the Colorsoft Signature Edition. Our <a href="/kindle-cover/#magnetic">cover guide</a> explains the magnetic-attach trade-off.</li>
    <li><strong>Page-Turn Cover ($79.99):</strong> a magnetic cover with physical page-turn buttons that connects through the pogo pins, for the Paperwhite and Colorsoft Signature Editions.</li>
    <li><strong>Third-party:</strong> at our check the 2026 Colorsoft had not shipped, so any third-party listing for it was made before owners could test fit. Look for reviews from owners after October 28.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="color">What a color screen changes about choosing a case</h2>
  <p>Less than you might expect. We looked for anything Amazon or independent reviewers say about cases and color displays specifically, and here is what we found, and did not find.</p>
  <Table
    caption="Color-screen questions and what our sources say."
    head={['Question', 'What we found', 'Source']}
    rows={[
      [`Does a case change how color looks?`, `No source says it does. A folio covers the screen only when closed.`, `None found`],
      [`Is the Colorsoft screen different from a Paperwhite's?`, `Yes. Amazon says a color filter layer means "the texture or brightness" may look different; 300 ppi in black and white, 150 ppi in color.`, `Amazon listing`],
      [`Does the case lining matter?`, `Amazon's case uses a "plush microfiber interior to help protect your screen from scratches."`, `Amazon case listing`],
      [`Will a case block the front light or add glare?`, `We found no source on this. The front light is built into the display, which Amazon describes as glare-free.`, `None found`],
      [`Should I add a screen protector?`, `Listings exist for the 2024 Paperwhite and Colorsoft, but we found no tests of their effect on color, light or glare.`, `Retail listings only`],
      [`Does a case cause or fix screen tint?`, `Amazon's review summary for the 2024 Colorsoft says many customers report a yellow tint at the bottom of the screen. That is reported as a display issue; a case is not a fix, and some reviewers say Amazon replaced affected units.`, `Amazon customer reviews`],
    ]}
  />
  <p>So the color screen itself is not a reason to pick a different case. The real Colorsoft-specific factors are the Signature Edition features in the next section. If you are weighing a screen protector, our <a href="/kindle-paperwhite-case/#screen-protector">screen protector notes</a> apply to the shared 2024 body, with the added unknown of how a protector interacts with the color filter layer, which we could not verify.</p>

  <h2 id="signature">Signature Edition features and cases</h2>
  <p>These are the features where a case can get in the way, by model.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Double Tap (2024 and 2026 Signature Editions).</strong> Amazon's 2024 Colorsoft guide describes accelerometer-based tap detection: tap twice quickly on the side or back, outside the screen, to go forward. It adds that the feature "has been tested with the official Amazon Kindle Colorsoft case, but may not work with all third party cases." If you rely on it, that is a reason to start with Amazon's case or to test a third-party case within its return window. Our <a href="/kindle-page-turner/#double-tap">page turner guide</a> covers the feature.</li>
    <li><strong>Qi wireless charging (2024 Signature Edition).</strong> The user guide says it charges on "any compatible Qi-certified wireless charger," then lists ten Qi-certified chargers that do not work with it because of "mechanical incompatibility." Amazon's wireless dock for it states a 4 mm case limit, and Amazon's safety text says to keep metallic or magnetic objects, including metallic cases, off the charger. A thin, non-metal case is the safest pairing.</li>
    <li><strong>Pogo pins (2026 Signature Edition).</strong> The contacts on the back connect to Amazon's $59.99 Charging Dock and the $79.99 Page-Turn Cover. A case that covers them blocks both.</li>
    <li><strong>USB-C (2024 and 2025 models; 2026 Signature Edition per The Verge).</strong> Amazon's plant-based case can stay on while charging. For third-party cases, check the cutout. Our <a href="/kindle-charger/">Kindle charger guide</a> lists Amazon's charge times and adapters for the Colorsoft.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The 16 GB models have none of the first three, so for them the choice is about fit, style and the USB-C cutout.</p>

  <h2 id="official">Amazon's own Colorsoft cases</h2>
  <Table
    caption="Amazon-made covers for Colorsoft models. Prices are Amazon.com snapshots and vary by color."
    head={['Cover', 'Fits (per Amazon)', 'Notable details', 'Price we saw']}
    rows={[
      [`Plant-based leather case (2024)`, `2024 Paperwhite, 2024 Paperwhite Signature, Kindle Colorsoft and Colorsoft Signature Edition`, `Microfiber interior; magnetic closure; opens and closes like a book to wake or sleep the Kindle; folds back; can stay on while charging; over 70% renewable bio-materials, rest polyurethane; Black, Raspberry, Jade`, `$42.99 (Raspberry), Oct 5, 2026`],
      [`2026 Kindle Covers`, `2026 lineup, color-matched`, `Knit fabric, plant-based leather or pebbled premium leather; wrap fully around the device`, `From $39.99 (announcement)`],
      [`2026 slim magnetic-attach covers`, `Aluminum models, including the Colorsoft Signature Edition`, `Device attaches magnetically rather than wrapping`, `Not stated in the announcement`],
      [`Page-Turn Cover (2026)`, `Paperwhite and Colorsoft Signature Editions`, `Physical page-turn buttons over pogo pins`, `$79.99 (announcement)`],
      [`Scribe Colorsoft folios`, `2025 Scribe and Scribe Colorsoft`, `See the <a href="/kindle-scribe-case/#y2025">Scribe guide</a>`, `See the Scribe guide`],
    ]}
  />
  <p>The 2024 plant-based case had 4.6 stars from 6,898 ratings when we checked. Amazon's review summary says owners like its fit, color and feel, while opinions on value and on how leather-like the material feels are mixed, with some saying it feels like hard plastic. That is a summary of other people's opinions, not our test. Third-party cases are cheaper and more varied, and we do not rank them.</p>
  <p><a class="btn alt" href={amazonDp('B0CM79Z8TG')} rel={LINK_REL} target="_blank">See Amazon's plant-based case</a></p>

  <h2 id="styles">Case styles for a Colorsoft</h2>
  <p>General case styles are compared in our <a href="/kindle-case/#types">case styles table</a> and the <a href="/kindle-cover/">cover guide</a>. This table only adds the Colorsoft-specific columns.</p>
  <Table
    caption="Our reasoning about Colorsoft features, not test results."
    head={['Style', 'Double Tap (Signature)', 'Wireless / dock charging', 'Good for']}
    rows={[
      [`Amazon folio`, `Tested by Amazon (2024 Colorsoft case)`, `Thin; can stay on for USB-C charging`, `Signature owners who use Double Tap`],
      [`Third-party hard-back folio`, `Not verified; may vary`, `Check thickness and any metal or magnet plate before wireless charging`, `Everyday bag carry, often with a stand or strap`],
      [`Slim shell or sleeve-style back`, `Not verified`, `Thin backs are the best bet on a Qi pad (2024); must leave pogo pins clear (2026)`, `Reading at home with some grip`],
      [`Magnetic-attach cover (2026 aluminum)`, `Not verified`, `Lifts off for the dock`, `People who dock nightly`],
      [`Page-Turn Cover (2026 Signature)`, `Physical buttons instead`, `Uses the pogo pins itself`, `Readers who want buttons`],
      [`Kids cover`, `Not verified`, `USB-C`, `Kindle Colorsoft Kids, which comes with a cover`],
    ]}
  />

  <h2 id="scribe">Kindle Scribe Colorsoft</h2>
  <p>The Scribe Colorsoft shares the Colorsoft name and display technology but not the size: it is an 11-inch writing tablet at 189 × 245 × 5.4 mm and 400 g by Amazon's figures, with the Premium Pen attached magnetically to the right side. Its cases are Scribe cases, with pen loops or flaps and attention to the pen magnet, and Amazon's listing says it charges in less than 3 hours with a 20W USB-C adapter. We cover it model by model, including what we could not confirm about whether it shares cases with the 2025 black-and-white Scribe, in the <a href="/kindle-scribe-case/#y2025">Kindle Scribe case guide</a>, so we do not repeat it here.</p>
  <p><a class="btn alt" href={amazonSearch('kindle scribe colorsoft case')} rel={LINK_REL} target="_blank">Search Amazon: Scribe Colorsoft cases</a></p>

  <h2 id="red-flags">Colorsoft case red flags</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>"Colorsoft case" with no screen size.</strong> It may be for the 11-inch Scribe Colorsoft.</li>
    <li><strong>One listing for "all Colorsoft" spanning 2024 and 2026.</strong> The 2026 body is thinner with the button in a different place.</li>
    <li><strong>Only "Paperwhite" in the title.</strong> A 2024 Paperwhite case may fit, but a listing that names the Colorsoft is safer, and a 2021 or 2026 Paperwhite case will not.</li>
    <li><strong>Metal plates or strong magnets in the back</strong> if you charge a 2024 Signature Edition wirelessly.</li>
    <li><strong>Coverage over the pogo pins</strong> on a 2026 Signature Edition if you want the dock or Page-Turn Cover.</li>
    <li><strong>"Official" or "Amazon certified"</strong> on a non-Amazon product. We cannot verify it and do not use that language ourselves.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="method">How we researched this</h2>
  <p>This guide uses Amazon.com listings for the 2024 Colorsoft Signature Edition, the 2024 Paperwhite, the Scribe Colorsoft and Amazon's plant-based leather case; Amazon's 2024 Colorsoft user guide; Amazon's July 2025 Colorsoft announcement and its October 1, 2026 lineup announcement; and coverage from The Verge and WIRED. We have not tested any case, and we do not rank third-party products. Prices and ratings are snapshots from {FACTS_AS_OF_OCT5}. Where a detail is unpublished, such as the 2026 Colorsoft's width and height, we say so. To report a mistake, use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>; our approach is described in the <a href="/about/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
  <ul class="sources">
    <li>Amazon.com, Kindle Colorsoft Signature Edition (2024) listing: size, weight, display notes, charging, generation, review summary.</li>
    <li>Amazon.com, Kindle Paperwhite (2024) listing: size and weight for comparison.</li>
    <li>Amazon.com, Amazon Plant-Based Leather Case for Kindle Paperwhite and Kindle Colorsoft: compatibility, materials, price, ratings.</li>
    <li>Amazon Kindle Colorsoft user guide: Double Tap and case testing note, Qi wireless charging, incompatible Qi chargers.</li>
    <li>Amazon, "Amazon expands Kindle Colorsoft family with 16 GB model" (July 24, 2025, updated 2026).</li>
    <li>Amazon, "The new Amazon Kindle lineup" (Oct 1, 2026); The Verge and WIRED, Oct 1, 2026: 2026 Colorsoft, covers, pogo pins, power button, thickness and weight.</li>
    <li>Best Buy listing of a tempered-glass screen protector for the 2024 Paperwhite and Colorsoft (example of grouping only).</li>
  </ul>

